.TH "FWD STOP" "1" "2026-08-12" "fwdit" "fwd stop Manual"
.SH NAME
fwd\-stop \- Check the remote Git worktree, kill tmux, and suspend
billable compute while retaining configured persistent storage.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fwd stop
[OPTIONS] [names]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Check the remote Git worktree, kill tmux, and suspend billable compute
while retaining configured persistent storage.
.PP
Restart with 'fwd attach --restart' or another 'fwd up'. Persistent
RunPod sessions retain their independent volume while terminating
disposable compute.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f,\fP \-\-force
Stop even if the remote Git worktree is dirty or cannot be inspected.
.SH EXIT STATUS
\fB0\fP indicates success. Any nonzero value indicates an error.
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report issues at \fIhttps://github.com/Sid-MB/fwd/issues\fP.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfwd\fP(1)
